---
import { docsNavigation } from "../../data/docs";
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";

const paths = [
  {
    label: "Application developer",
    title: "Add passkeys to an app",
    body: "Start the standalone stack, complete a ceremony, exchange the session for a JWT and verify it in your API.",
    href: "/docs/integration",
  },
  {
    label: "Platform operator",
    title: "Deploy one isolated realm",
    body: "Understand the three-service topology, versioned configuration, secrets, backups and recovery gates.",
    href: "/docs/deployment",
  },
  {
    label: "Fleet operator",
    title: "Manage many realms",
    body: "Run the separate Fleet control plane and pair organizations, projects and environments without sharing databases.",
    href: "/docs/fleet",
  },
];
---

<DocsLayout title="Own the identity boundary." eyebrow="RustyAuth documentation" intro="Learn, integrate and operate RustyAuth—from one isolated realm to a cross-cloud Fleet control plane.">
  <div class="docs-status-strip" aria-label="Project status">
    <div><small>Release</small><strong>0.1.0 pre-release</strong></div>
    <div><small>Runtime</small><strong>Rust + Dioxus + SableDB</strong></div>
    <div><small>Production gate</small><strong>Security review required</strong></div>
  </div>

  <div class="doc-callout warning">
    <strong>Evaluate before production</strong>
    <p>Passkeys, revocable sessions, Fleet hierarchy and encrypted recovery are implemented. Account recovery, abuse controls, multi-writer qualification and an independent security assessment are not complete.</p>
  </div>

  <h2>Choose your path</h2>
  <div class="docs-path-grid">
    {paths.map((path) => (
      <a class="docs-card" href={path.href}>
        <small>{path.label}</small>
        <h3>{path.title}</h3>
        <p>{path.body}</p>
        <span>Follow the path →</span>
      </a>
    ))}
  </div>

  <h2>The product boundary</h2>
  <p>RustyAuth authenticates an identity, maintains revocable browser sessions and issues short-lived claims for downstream services. Your application still owns authorization, roles, entitlements and resource ownership.</p>
  <div class="doc-architecture">
    <div><small>Presentation</small><strong>Dioxus dashboard</strong><span>Web · desktop · mobile</span></div>
    <b>→</b>
    <div class="accent"><small>Trust boundary</small><strong>RustyAuth API</strong><span>Passkeys · policy · Protobuf</span></div>
    <b>→</b>
    <div class="dark"><small>Private state</small><strong>SableDB</strong><span>Durable realm or Fleet data</span></div>
  </div>

  <h2>Browse every guide</h2>
  <div class="docs-card-grid">
    {docsNavigation.flatMap((group) => group.items.filter((item) => item.href !== "/docs").map((item) => (
      <a class="docs-card" href={item.href}>
        <small>{group.label}</small>
        <h3>{item.label}</h3>
        <p>{item.description}</p>
        <span>Open guide →</span>
      </a>
    )))}
  </div>

  <h2>Source of truth</h2>
  <p>This site is the guided developer experience. The repository contains the normative protocol, security and operational references. Start at the <a href="https://github.com/rusty-auth/rustyauth/blob/main/docs/README.md">GitHub documentation index</a> when you need exhaustive contracts or release-specific detail.</p>
</DocsLayout>
